{"ok": true, "command": "retrieve", "result": {"stopping_reason": "BUDGET_EXHAUSTED_WITH_GAPS", "evidence": [{"id": "EXP-003-examin", "sha256": "7be1a4a25d7a25724fe81e9a8dabe334ac9b3070d59cb90e686fa4329ef6c99b", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 8, "text": "---\nid: EXP-003-examin\ntype: research\nstatus: ACTIVE\nstate_class: EVIDENCE\ntitle: EXAMIN profile on a clone of the owner's copy at a7cf346 (EXP-003's EXAMIN leg, W2-26)\n---\n\n", "chunk_id": "504af939b2c2d3a4d5402b55", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "EXP-003-examin", "sha256": "2b7feee85c6241229743c6752b64b25b9d6689a69e4111d0567a7e3cbcab2022", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 17, "text": "## Question\n\nWhat does EXAMIN's committed tree look like for adoption, measured on a clone of the owner's copy? This covers its size, its languages, its test runner(s) and their commands, and its suite's wall time. It also covers each index's time and peak RSS as this repository's `gov` builds them, against DEC-078's envelope, and whether a path with a space breaks any command (W2-I041). Two consequences are reported, not decided: W2-19 joins W2-27 if EXAMIN's tests are not pytest (DEC-727), and W2-45 joins W2-27 if something exceeds its budget at EXAMIN's size.\n\n", "chunk_id": "ed84ba59bfc415cbde3e15e5", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "EXP-003-examin", "sha256": "d7c3f431f59e77c9e9f123b0960039a2b1a7b1f5fb9154fd4cf8dd5fc5271a91", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 35, "text": "## Method\n\n1. **The clone (DEC-723, DEC-728).** The owner's copy was read by one command only. No other command listed, read or wrote the workbench, and none touched EXAMIN's real repository:\n   `/usr/bin/time -v git clone --no-hardlinks /home/usain/gov-os-workbench/examin /tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin` (exit 0, 0.12 s). Its head is `a7cf346` (`a7cf346c28d7ba7b9edf8a18e1bb6e20ab1b19ca`).\n2. **The uncommitted entries.** The owner's copy carries 9 uncommitted entries (6 modified, 3 untracked), and a clone does not see them. This profile measures the committed tree at `a7cf346`. The owner is to give the entries' paths for Q-16 (W2-29). By the orchestrator's decision, which is stricter than the ticket's O-1 section, no `git status` or other command ran in the copy, so this record does not name them.\n3. **Size and languages**, all with `git -C <clone> ...`: `ls-files | wc -l`, `rev-list --count HEAD`, tracked bytes (`stat` over `ls-files`, and blob sizes from `ls-tree -l`), and lines from `git diff --numstat <empty tree> HEAD`. That diff uses git's own binary detection (a binary shows `-`), so binaries count as files and bytes but not as lines. The extension table is grouped from the same numstat. Commands are in [`raw/size.txt`](raw/size.txt) and [`raw/languages.tsv`](raw/languages.tsv).\n4. **Test runners.** Test configuration and documentation were found by name over `git ls-files` and read; only their test command lines are quoted ([`raw/test-runners.txt`](raw/test-runners.txt)).\n5. **Suite wall time.** A suite was run only if it needed no install, network service, container, database or credential. The **governance suite** qualified and ran on each clone with EXAMIN's runner's own pytest line, `/usr/bin/time -v` and `timeout 1800`, in the background. It used `/usr/bin/python3` 3.12.3, and `PYTHONPATH` was removed for it (DEC-732 does not apply to EXAMIN's suite). The **product suite** did not qualify and was not started ([`raw/product-suite-needs.txt`](raw/product-suite-needs.txt)).\n6. **Indexing (DEC-732, DEC-719).**\n   - The code under test is this worktree's `src/`. Every `gov` command and direct call carried the absolute prefix `PYTHONPATH=/home/usain/gov-os-worktrees/W2-26/src`.\n   - The primary run was the full rebuild (never `--no-embeddings`), `--root` on the clone, under `/usr/bin/time -v`.\n   - A sampler wrote the pid, ppid, RSS and command of every `codebase-memory-mcp`, `gitleaks` and gov process every 2 s, so that the tool's daemon and worker would be counted if they ran.\n   - Then gov's three index functions were timed as **direct calls**, unmodified and one at a time.\n   - No path map, `.gitleaks.toml` or other governance file was written into either clone, and neither was adopted.\n7. **The path with a space (W2-I041).** A second clone was made **from the first clone**: `git clone --no-hardlinks /tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin \"/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/EXAMIN APP\"`. Every measure above ran there again, with the path quoted, and its outputs were compared with the first clone's.\n\nEvery long run went in the background with an exit-code file under `/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/runs/`, one run at a time.\n\n", "chunk_id": "c446a940960f55f71ea1f825", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "WAVE-2-WBS", "sha256": "4692c4295f9d3863d7b35d6a683e053a6dd46d413291ae80f921e61006475f67", "path": "docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md", "start_line": 723, "end_line": 737, "text": "#### W2-26 EXAMIN profile on the owner's copy: EXP-003's EXAMIN leg (STANDARD, research)\n- **Needs first:** the owner's copy at `~/gov-os-workbench/examin/`, made in a plain terminal, and its exact path (owner act O-1).\n- **Allowed paths:** `docs/research/EXP-003/examin/**`, plus a working clone made with `git clone --no-hardlinks` from the exact path:\n  - before W2-50 closes, the clone goes in a folder of its own under `/tmp`, by literal path (`/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin/`); it is throwaway, and every result is committed under `docs/research/EXP-003/examin/` (DEC-728);\n  - after W2-50 closes, it goes under `~/gov-os-runs/W2-26/examin/`.\n  The owner's copy is read only by that clone; nothing in the workbench is listed or written.\n- **KPIs:**\n  - On the working clone: size (files, lines, tracked bytes, commits), languages, test runner(s) and their commands, and the test suite's wall time.\n  - Indexing time and peak RSS for each index, against DEC-078's envelope.\n  - Whether the path with a space breaks any command [W2-I041].\n- **Consequences:**\n  - If its tests are not pytest, W2-19 joins W2-27's dependencies (DEC-727).\n  - If the decision checker or `gov check` exceeds its budget at EXAMIN's size, W2-45 joins them too.\n- **Runs** beside W2-01 (layer 1), and **closes** after W2-07.\n\n", "chunk_id": "97e37ce8b413dfdb77309df2", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "EXP-003-examin", "sha256": "076e3c40846d26440195e01dbfc0631dec75474c71c9f28371990d13c0c92359", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 9, "end_line": 13, "text": "# EXP-003-examin \u2014 EXAMIN profile on a clone of the owner's copy at a7cf346\n\n- **Ticket:** `DAEO-2ds6` (W2-26, STANDARD, research). **Sources:** DEC-728, DEC-078, DEC-727; DEC-719, DEC-723, DEC-725, DEC-673, DEC-732.\n- **Run:** 2026-10-16, 17:27 to about 17:55 UTC, by one headless research session, on this machine. Raw outputs are in [`raw/`](raw/).\n\n", "chunk_id": "5de55ad3d7ae3371b862cc63", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "EXP-003-examin", "sha256": "3ee6e9f49e7a0a16b9d6bec6f118976b89132b0b494254edaaa66786d867b51e", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 127, "end_line": 138, "text": "### The path with a space (W2-I041)\n\n| Command on `\"/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/EXAMIN APP\"` | Exit | Same as on `/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin`? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `git clone --no-hardlinks /tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin \"/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/EXAMIN APP\"` | 0 (0.12 s) | \u2014 |\n| size and language measures (`ls-files`, `rev-list`, `stat`, `diff --numstat`) | 0 | yes: identical numbers; `cmp` of the two numstat files finds no difference |\n| governance suite | 1 (1:15.7) | yes: 828 / 15 / 165, the identical set of failing test ids (`comm` finds none in only one run) |\n| `gov rebuild --root \"\u2026EXAMIN APP\" --json` | 0 (0.50 s, 58.9 MB) | yes: the same three `not_recreated` reasons, the path in the message carrying the space |\n| the three direct calls | 1 each | yes: the same `RuntimeError`, the spaced path in its text |\n\n**No command broke on the space.** The space did change one thing: in gov's messages, the path with a space is printed inside quotes, unescaped.\n\n", "chunk_id": "d868730d13eb3d99b2d65e66", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DEC-950", "sha256": "50072992525d7452536fe39a4e3a68f42de265c61772f437c48af9f63d619d92", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 7694, "end_line": 7701, "text": "### DEC-723 \u2014 The EXAMIN profile runs early and read-only on a copy the owner makes; agents never write, list, glob or search in `~/gov-os-workbench` (P-W2-4 (a))\n- **Status:** ACCEPTED (owner, 2026-10-16; the owner commits this entry with `Role: owner`) \u00b7 **Under:** DEC-718, DEC-525 \u00b7 **Basis:** EXAMIN's size, languages and test runner decide whether Track B waits for the language-agnostic test commands and the check runner's scale work; measuring them early sizes that work before it is built. In the planning session, a listing of the workbench folder printed a protected folder's name (nothing in it was read).\n- **Decision:**\n  1. W2-26 (the EXAMIN profile, EXP-003's EXAMIN leg) runs early, beside Track A, read-only.\n  2. **The owner makes the copy** at `~/gov-os-workbench/examin/` in a plain terminal and gives the orchestrator its exact path.\n  3. **Agents never write in `~/gov-os-workbench`.** Work that writes (indexing, test runs, adoption on a copy) runs on a clone the agent makes outside it, under `~/gov-os-runs/<W2 id>/`, from the exact path the owner gave.\n  4. **Agents never list, glob or search `~/gov-os-workbench`.** They name a file there explicitly, or ask the owner.\n\n", "chunk_id": "80c8b89c68c4635dbf669f25", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DAEO-2ds6", "sha256": "e8c4137f6c4ae4d6b7dfcb0ce3867170019a9437d7dd4971914a6cb023fc3b91", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-2ds6.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 42, "text": "---\nid: DAEO-2ds6\nstatus: in_progress\ndeps: []\nlinks: []\ncreated: 2026-10-16T16:35:11Z\ntype: task\npriority: 1\nassignee: research\nexternal-ref: W2-26\ntags: [wave-2, research, standard]\nwbs_id: W2-26\ntitle: EXAMIN profile on the owner's copy (EXP-003's EXAMIN leg)\nclass: research\nstate_class: AUTHORITATIVE\nrole: research\ndepends_on: []\nallowed_paths:\n- docs/research/EXP-003/examin/**\nkpis:\n  success:\n  - 'On the working clone: size (files, lines, tracked bytes, commits), languages, test runner(s) and their commands, and the test suite''s wall time.'\n  - Indexing time and peak RSS for each index, against DEC-078's envelope.\n  - Whether the path with a space breaks any command [W2-I041].\n  failure: []\nprofile: STANDARD\nsources:\n- DEC-728\n- DEC-078\n- DEC-727\nest_loc: 60\nacceptance_tests:\n  evidence:\n  - docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md\n  judged_by: 'its class (WBS \u00a70 rule 1, W2-07): its evidence record'\ntrack: B\ncloses:\n- EXP-003 (EXAMIN)\n- W2-I041\nlist_rows:\n- W2-I041\n---\n", "chunk_id": "03ca28be46a0bfed84d81c30", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "679a6e890761e40b698e151d", "sha256": "dea5b3634730de53d3424808b081aea8ed7b684524d136f6a12add7d47907c7d", "path": "docs/assessment/2026-10/SYNTHESIS.md", "start_line": 210, "end_line": 231, "text": "### Phase 4. Use on EXAMIN's copy\n\n- **Covers.** W2-26 (the EXAMIN profile, the research leg of EXP-003), W2-27 (the adoption of the copy) and W2-28 (the independent verdict) [Charter:33\u201334; D \u00a72.1].\n- **Entry.**\n  - Track A has passed and been audited (W2-25) [Charter:32\u201334].\n  - A pinned, hash-verified release exists [Charter:34].\n  - W2-49 has merged, so the copy is judged against Contract 4.2 [C R-4].\n  - Research can be launched (P-S6) [E F6].\n  - The proofs of section 6. B asks for them \"before any adoption\" [B].\n  - W2-24, W2-56 and W2-57 have closed, as DEC-794, DEC-799 and DEC-813 require. The WBS card states these conditions; they must also be written into W2-27's ticket file, as dependencies [A F3, F9].\n  - By DEC-803, the risks that come with running agents in another repository:\n    - the kernel's lead rules are brought up to Wave 2 (W2-11) [C F-9];\n    - leads are sandboxed under their own role (W2-21), if W2-27 does not list it already [E F1].\n- **Exit evidence.** W2-28's verdict is ADOPTED_HEALTHY, or ADOPTED_WITH_ACCEPTED_EXCEPTIONS, against CAP-44.h's lite conditions. These include:\n  - `gov doctor` MATCH with the pinned release, and `gov doctor` green;\n  - `gov check` with no RED family;\n  - one ticket closed by `gov close` at exit 0, with the repository's own test command [CAP-44.h].\n- **Estimate.** 3 to 6 working days after W2-25's verdict.\n  - The plan put the copy's verdict a day before Track A's (day 13 against day 14) [D \u00a72.3].\n  - Three later owner decisions put W2-27 after W2-24 [A F3].\n  - The Charter's wording puts the pilot after Track A's audit (P-S8 raises this).\n\n", "chunk_id": "679a6e890761e40b698e151d", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DAEO-h4rh", "sha256": "aa0ca318ce7a30be0c6580a70505c2eafcdf2443059781588c9e7317ebadd20c", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-h4rh.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 72, "text": "---\nid: DAEO-h4rh\nstatus: open\ndeps: [DAEO-g0ip, DAEO-ym8a, DAEO-u4oz, DAEO-0z8c, DAEO-kia7, DAEO-7r5e, DAEO-a3m2, DAEO-cuao, DAEO-49o5, DAEO-057v, DAEO-r30l, DAEO-1ahb, DAEO-kmcr, DAEO-2ds6, DAEO-ha8z, DAEO-kl5e, DAEO-jzvg, DAEO-siiz]\nlinks: []\ncreated: 2026-10-16T16:35:11Z\ntype: task\npriority: 1\nassignee: orchestrator\nexternal-ref: W2-27\ntags: [wave-2, integration, full]\nwbs_id: W2-27\ntitle: EXAMIN adoption on a copy\nclass: integration\nstate_class: AUTHORITATIVE\nrole: orchestrator\ndepends_on:\n- DAEO-g0ip\n- DAEO-ym8a\n- DAEO-u4oz\n- DAEO-0z8c\n- DAEO-kia7\n- DAEO-7r5e\n- DAEO-a3m2\n- DAEO-cuao\n- DAEO-49o5\n- DAEO-057v\n- DAEO-r30l\n- DAEO-1ahb\n- DAEO-kmcr\n- DAEO-2ds6\n- DAEO-ha8z\n- DAEO-kl5e\n- DAEO-jzvg\n- DAEO-siiz\nallowed_paths:\n- docs/plan/wave-2/examin-copy/**\nkpis:\n  success:\n  - The pinned, hash-verified release is installed (W2-16, W2-18).\n  - gov adopt runs A0 to A6 and A8 with the A5 independent review, and the lite A7 and A10 gates of Contract v4.2.\n  - EXAMIN's own CLAUDE.md, settings and untracked files are preserved (W2-23).\n  - gov doctor and gov check are green.\n  - 'One LITE ticket goes through the full cycle: test designer, red, implement, green, then gov close at exit 0 with EXAMIN''s own test command.'\n  - Its governance share is measured and \u2264 15 %.\n  - At the first full gov rebuild after adoption, each index's time, peak RSS and node and edge counts on EXAMIN are measured with W2-26's method and RSS sampler, against DEC-078's envelope; a figure over the envelope stops the ticket, and W2-45 joins its dependencies [DEC-735].\n  - Before any known-red list, a diagnosis hour sorts EXAMIN's red tests into environment reds and real ones; the owner does not know whether its governance suite passes on Windows, so the hour finds out (DEC-745).\n    Then the reds go into W2-19's ratchet baseline (exact id, owner, cause class, how it shrinks), which the owner accepts [DEC-736].\n  - One pinned install package goes to the owner. It holds EXAMIN's 10 product-suite packages from EXAMIN's own lock file, installed into the clone's own virtual environment only. With the owner's approval,\n    the product suite is measured before W2-30's verdict. Until then it is \"needs environment\", reported UNMEASURED by name and never as passed [DEC-736].\n  - EXAMIN's governance kit stays in a legacy namespace, and its tests stay in the declared test command. The A5 review maps each of its checks to a Gov OS check family or to \"no equivalent\" [DEC-736].\n  - The path map marks the tool-configuration folders (.claude/commands/ and the kit's .claude/ templates) as not records. The files in spec/5-REPORTS/attempts/ get a mechanical quoting fix of their front\n    matter with no change of content, as an adoption commit. If the store cannot leave paths unread, all 18 files get the fix [DEC-736].\n  - EXAMIN's own CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and .claude/commands/ are never silently overwritten. Their content is migrated into EXAMIN's rulesync sources or kept in place, and the A5 review checks that nothing\n    of the owner's was lost [DEC-736].\n  failure: []\nprofile: FULL\nsources:\n- DEC-727\n- DEC-728\n- DEC-735\n- DEC-736\n- DEC-741\n- DEC-745\nest_loc: 0\nacceptance_tests:\n  judged_by: 'its class (WBS \u00a70 rule 1, W2-07): its named evidence files'\ntrack: B\ncloses:\n- Track B\nlist_rows: []\n---\n", "chunk_id": "0b99bbe9c29f2235d8bb02f0", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DAEO-2ds6", "sha256": "8deabc582a39474ec64916c17b7d6adc011c55582945f86f53734b9371b28c38", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-2ds6.md", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 60, "text": "# W2-26 EXAMIN profile on the owner's copy (EXP-003's EXAMIN leg)\n\nCard: `docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md` \u00a72 (W2-26), as approved (DEC-729). The list rows it takes in are in `list_rows` and in `docs/plan/WAVE_2_TRIAGE.md`; a row's state is re-checked against the code when the ticket picks it up (DEC-718).\n\n- **Needs first:** the owner's copy at `~/gov-os-workbench/examin/`, made in a plain terminal, and its exact path (owner act O-1).\n- **Allowed paths:** `docs/research/EXP-003/examin/**`, plus a working clone made with `git clone --no-hardlinks` from the exact path:\n  - before W2-50 closes, the clone goes in a folder of its own under `/tmp`, by literal path (`/tmp/gov-os-W2-26/examin/`); it is throwaway, and every result is committed under `docs/research/EXP-003/examin/` (DEC-728);\n  - after W2-50 closes, it goes under `~/gov-os-runs/W2-26/examin/`.\n  The owner's copy is read only by that clone; nothing in the workbench is listed or written.\n- **KPIs:**\n  - On the working clone: size (files, lines, tracked bytes, commits), languages, test runner(s) and their commands, and the test suite's wall time.\n  - Indexing time and peak RSS for each index, against DEC-078's envelope.\n  - Whether the path with a space breaks any command [W2-I041].\n- **Consequences:**\n  - If its tests are not pytest, W2-19 joins W2-27's dependencies (DEC-727).\n  - If the decision checker or `gov check` exceeds its budget at EXAMIN's size, W2-45 joins them too.\n- **Runs** beside W2-01 (layer 1), and **closes** after W2-07.\n\n", "chunk_id": "1ea9180cc90580594a898351", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "316caf2a359830c3d96212af", "sha256": "7e5641701231b43132211585311d7975a1f298361cc28196a0fceb849441fb0f", "path": "docs/assessment/2026-10/SYNTHESIS.md", "start_line": 75, "end_line": 82, "text": "| DEC-105's three options | A proposal that contradicts a closed specification comes with three costed options: apply now, defer, or re-baseline [D \u00a71]. |\n| Scratch | `.gov-runtime/scratch/`, a working folder that git ignores [C F-1]. |\n| EXAMIN's copy, EXAMIN's real repository | The owner's copy of the EXAMIN product, used for the trial adoption (W2-27, verdict by W2-28), and the product's real repository (verdict by W2-30) [Charter:32\u201336]. |\n\n**Limits.**\n1. **Second-hand evidence.** I read only the sources above. Every fact about code, the register, the plan and the logs comes through the reports' own citations, which I did not re-check.\n2. **Nothing re-measured.** Where the reports disagree, I say so, with the evidence each rests on, and I do not settle it (Appendix A).\n3. **Estimates are mine.** The time estimates in section 2 are my judgement. I state their basis and my confidence.\n", "chunk_id": "316caf2a359830c3d96212af", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "WAVE-2-WBS", "sha256": "6b4b4400c9b4c4f72ba57c2d870e34180b8ba291f0b446890591e3b53672df66", "path": "docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md", "start_line": 711, "end_line": 722, "text": "### Track B \u2014 the EXAMIN pilot\n\n**K9's entry criteria (owner, DEC-941 items 3, 6 and 7):**\n- **For EXAMIN's copy:**\n  - memory measured: W2-61's standing measure at DEC-833's floor on the pinned stores;\n  - the adoption proving ground passed (W2-81);\n  - Wave 2-grade evidence (a clean close, the memory measure, or the proving ground) for every capability the copy relies on, not only Wave 1's record.\n  - a Definition of Ready checked at claim (W2-82, `DAEO-4k3l`) and a playbook per stream in the kernel template (W2-83a, `DAEO-dy7j`) (owner, DEC-944 items 2 and 3).\n- **For EXAMIN's real repository:** the same, and a release path (K7: W2-16 closed and a release cut and hash-verified).\n\nEXAMIN's real repository is never written before W2-25 passes, W2-15b reports, W2-28's verdict is in, and the owner gives the go (DEC-727). Before that, every EXAMIN step works on clones under `~/gov-os-runs/`, made from the owner's copy by its exact path (DEC-723). The one exception is W2-26's throwaway `/tmp` clone, before W2-50 (DEC-728).\n\n", "chunk_id": "c0ca13c36773ecb8712400f6", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DAEO-h4rh", "sha256": "4240c5ef54566169934155f9ac5975f80a8f70357b9c723235bb6f4e91f0692a", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-h4rh.md", "start_line": 54, "end_line": 72, "text": "  - EXAMIN's own CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and .claude/commands/ are never silently overwritten. Their content is migrated into EXAMIN's rulesync sources or kept in place, and the A5 review checks that nothing\n    of the owner's was lost [DEC-736].\n  failure: []\nprofile: FULL\nsources:\n- DEC-727\n- DEC-728\n- DEC-735\n- DEC-736\n- DEC-741\n- DEC-745\nest_loc: 0\nacceptance_tests:\n  judged_by: 'its class (WBS \u00a70 rule 1, W2-07): its named evidence files'\ntrack: B\ncloses:\n- Track B\nlist_rows: []\n---\n", "chunk_id": "0fe7c28837c8395b0f08a0f2", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DAEO-h4rh", "sha256": "9ba43ab001016af9fcee6047a80ab7395ae34a132ca38e982854c23cdae0ac76", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-h4rh.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 43, "text": "---\nid: DAEO-h4rh\nstatus: open\ndeps: [DAEO-g0ip, DAEO-ym8a, DAEO-u4oz, DAEO-0z8c, DAEO-kia7, DAEO-7r5e, DAEO-a3m2, DAEO-cuao, DAEO-49o5, DAEO-057v, DAEO-r30l, DAEO-1ahb, DAEO-kmcr, DAEO-2ds6, DAEO-ha8z, DAEO-kl5e, DAEO-jzvg, DAEO-siiz]\nlinks: []\ncreated: 2026-10-16T16:35:11Z\ntype: task\npriority: 1\nassignee: orchestrator\nexternal-ref: W2-27\ntags: [wave-2, integration, full]\nwbs_id: W2-27\ntitle: EXAMIN adoption on a copy\nclass: integration\nstate_class: AUTHORITATIVE\nrole: orchestrator\ndepends_on:\n- DAEO-g0ip\n- DAEO-ym8a\n- DAEO-u4oz\n- DAEO-0z8c\n- DAEO-kia7\n- DAEO-7r5e\n- DAEO-a3m2\n- DAEO-cuao\n- DAEO-49o5\n- DAEO-057v\n- DAEO-r30l\n- DAEO-1ahb\n- DAEO-kmcr\n- DAEO-2ds6\n- DAEO-ha8z\n- DAEO-kl5e\n- DAEO-jzvg\n- DAEO-siiz\nallowed_paths:\n- docs/plan/wave-2/examin-copy/**\nkpis:\n  success:\n  - The pinned, hash-verified release is installed (W2-16, W2-18).\n  - gov adopt runs A0 to A6 and A8 with the A5 independent review, and the lite A7 and A10 gates of Contract v4.2.\n  - EXAMIN's own CLAUDE.md, settings and untracked files are preserved (W2-23).\n  - gov doctor and gov check are green.\n", "chunk_id": "b520ef2b20daf7446682805a", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "WAVE-2-WBS", "sha256": "e50c90d8e19217d24134001c7afcf20e70d69bdfba944d02d2ba0140e279b1e7", "path": "docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md", "start_line": 738, "end_line": 750, "text": "#### W2-27 EXAMIN adoption on a copy (FULL, orchestrator)\n- **Depends on (DEC-727):** W2-01, W2-03, W2-04, W2-05, W2-06, W2-08, W2-09, W2-10, W2-16, W2-18, W2-20, W2-21 and W2-23; W2-26; W2-49 (the lite gates); W2-50 (the clone's folder, DEC-728); W2-19 (DEC-736); W2-52 (the lite A7 and A10 stage records, DEC-741); and W2-45 if the index measures say so (DEC-735). W2-07 lands before it by rule 1.\n- **DEC-794 (owner, 2026-10-18):** W2-27 does not start unless W2-24's repeat of the quality-control check gives sections (a) and (d) green: workers sandboxed through `gov launch`, and `gov retrieve` returning correct, deterministic results on this repository.\n- **DEC-799 (owner, 2026-10-19):** and W2-56 has closed.\n- **Allowed paths:** `docs/plan/wave-2/examin-copy/**` (evidence); the clone at `~/gov-os-runs/W2-27/examin/` only.\n- **KPIs:**\n  - The pinned, hash-verified release is installed (W2-16, W2-18).\n  - `gov adopt` runs A0 to A6 and A8 with the A5 independent review, and the lite A7 and A10 gates of Contract v4.2.\n  - EXAMIN's own `CLAUDE.md`, settings and untracked files are preserved (W2-23).\n  - `gov doctor` and `gov check` are green.\n  - One LITE ticket goes through the full cycle: test designer, red, implement, green, then `gov close` at exit 0 with EXAMIN's own test command.\n  - Its governance share is measured and \u2264 15 %.\n\n", "chunk_id": "3ea1e3e14e52774877b6a994", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DAEO-h4rh", "sha256": "96c224fcde7b589c643471c77a4ac2c21e99a96c2023052c6b73aeb9a9beb589", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-h4rh.md", "start_line": 82, "end_line": 87, "text": "  - EXAMIN's own `CLAUDE.md`, settings and untracked files are preserved (W2-23).\n  - `gov doctor` and `gov check` are green.\n  - One LITE ticket goes through the full cycle: test designer, red, implement, green, then `gov close` at exit 0 with EXAMIN's own test command.\n  - Its governance share is measured and \u2264 15 %.\n  - At the first full `gov rebuild` after adoption, each index's time, peak RSS and node and edge counts on EXAMIN are measured with W2-26's method and RSS sampler (`docs/research/EXP-003/examin/`), against DEC-078's envelope. A figure over the envelope stops the ticket, and W2-45 joins its dependencies [DEC-735].\n  - Before any known-red list, a diagnosis hour sorts EXAMIN's red tests into environment reds and real ones; the owner does not know whether its governance suite passes on Windows, so the hour finds out (DEC-745). Then the reds go into W2-19's ratchet baseline (exact id, owner, cause class, how it shrinks), which the owner accepts [DEC-736].\n", "chunk_id": "8c62d6051bad499b1c8e9ce7", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DAEO-h4rh", "sha256": "7e0029c8af63fa146cb3b942d260bc3c3b8eb7c66d42d41c679114abb7eccc47", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-h4rh.md", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 49, "text": "  - EXAMIN's own CLAUDE.md, settings and untracked files are preserved (W2-23).\n  - gov doctor and gov check are green.\n  - 'One LITE ticket goes through the full cycle: test designer, red, implement, green, then gov close at exit 0 with EXAMIN''s own test command.'\n  - Its governance share is measured and \u2264 15 %.\n  - At the first full gov rebuild after adoption, each index's time, peak RSS and node and edge counts on EXAMIN are measured with W2-26's method and RSS sampler, against DEC-078's envelope; a figure over the envelope stops the ticket, and W2-45 joins its dependencies [DEC-735].\n  - Before any known-red list, a diagnosis hour sorts EXAMIN's red tests into environment reds and real ones; the owner does not know whether its governance suite passes on Windows, so the hour finds out (DEC-745).\n    Then the reds go into W2-19's ratchet baseline (exact id, owner, cause class, how it shrinks), which the owner accepts [DEC-736].\n  - One pinned install package goes to the owner. It holds EXAMIN's 10 product-suite packages from EXAMIN's own lock file, installed into the clone's own virtual environment only. With the owner's approval,\n", "chunk_id": "e9005440a260e3c65e78f84a", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "WAVE-2-LIST", "sha256": "a4773101192dcee1319624afe76c4682f42ea8b87e3186e7451ae5202a10bd22", "path": "docs/plan/WAVE_2_LIST.md", "start_line": 608, "end_line": 610, "text": "| W2-M358 | EXAMIN's product suite has no reproducible environment of its own (10 packages, a bundled Postgres) | orchestrator | A Docker Compose environment (or the like) runs EXAMIN's whole product suite, the `slow` Postgres tests included, from one declared command. | P-W2-8 (b), 2026-10-16 (DEC-736) |\n| W2-M359 | A launched session's Write and Edit tools may not reach its own folder under `~/gov-os-runs` (Claude Code's own check of paths outside the working folder; DEC-313 refuses `--add-dir`), leaving Bash only | engineer | W2-21's launch work shows whether a launched worker's Write and Edit reach its own folder, and either they do or the launch states that only Bash writes there. | W2-50 CIT-P \u00a76.3, 2026-10-16 (DEC-743) |\n| W2-M360 | `gov close`'s accepted history trusts the register's text whoever committed it: an entry worded as the owner's, committed by an engineer, was accepted when the path map listed it | engineer | An accepted-history entry counts only when its decision entry was committed by an owner commit (`Role: owner`). | W2-01 probe of run 2, 2026-10-16 (DEC-757) |\n", "chunk_id": "0c5d0e7618c997d47da941a2", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DEC-950", "sha256": "0dfe9c9068b4e6a22cd3c6c0550305319540040938016e1a9984d5b0ebc92146", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 6098, "end_line": 6099, "text": "## 159. Owner answers to P-25, on EXP-001's evidence file, on the schema findings of probe records, on two findings of W1-30's close, and a Wave 2 item (register v0.159, appended by the W1 orchestrator on branch `w1/integrate`)\n\n", "chunk_id": "cb88bdf221d9ed33393a6223", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}], "batches": [{"size": 10}, {"size": 10}], "merge": {"candidates": 20, "duplicates": 0, "dropped": [], "reranked": true}, "expansions": [{"chunk_id": "c446a940960f55f71ea1f825", "parent_id": "8742f9249a68cd9d852aff98", "path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 35}, {"chunk_id": "97e37ce8b413dfdb77309df2", "parent_id": "2e7feed536879035e22ee165", "path": "docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md", "start_line": 723, "end_line": 737}, {"chunk_id": "679a6e890761e40b698e151d", "parent_id": "b5a33a576ae760476099b005", "path": "docs/assessment/2026-10/SYNTHESIS.md", "start_line": 210, "end_line": 231}, {"chunk_id": "0b99bbe9c29f2235d8bb02f0", "parent_id": "4f3c76afaf890622a0399e37", 